Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.35,0:00:07.19,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,You certainly enjoy your drink.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.42,0:00:10.86,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,What happened this afternoon \Nwas a disaster...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.72,0:00:13.99,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Behaving like like that in \Nfront of so many people...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.01,0:00:22.50,Italics - Top,Serafina,0,0,0,,Still... that was the first \Ntime a man ever protected me...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.73,0:00:27.06,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Personally, I think you're a lot more\N personable than you were before.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.09,0:00:32.97,Main - Top,Cersei,0,0,0,,I would've never believed that \Nthere are nobles willing to risk
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.97,0:00:34.26,Main - Top,Cersei,0,0,0,,their safety for others.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.94,0:00:36.31,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I'm going to get more liquor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.36,0:00:47.02,Main - Top,Serafina,0,0,0,,It's probably the alcohol... \Nbut this isn't so bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.02,0:00:52.40,Sign_Basic,series title,0,0,0,,{\an2\fs8\fnTimes New Roman\bord1\shad.5\b1\c&HFAFDFE&\3c&H3D6671&\4c&H372771&\pos(95,315)}The Warrior Princess and the Barbaric King
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.22,0:00:52.40,Italics - Top,Serafina,0,0,0,,Someone else protecting me...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.72,0:00:58.18,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,No, no! What am I thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.18,0:01:00.50,Main,Vyufmec,0,0,0,,Illodren's back!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.50,0:01:01.93,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Was that a child?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.68,0:01:04.54,Main,Vyufmec,0,0,0,,And Illdoren looked this way!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.82,0:01:10.04,Main,Fairy A,0,0,0,,She spurted!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.04,0:01:11.48,Main - Top,Fairy B,0,0,0,,Hilarious.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.52,0:01:14.74,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,D-Did I drink to the point \Nof hallucinating...?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.74,0:01:17.54,Main,Fairy Trio,0,0,0,,It's Illdoren, Illdoren!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.54,0:01:19.78,Main,Fairy Trio,0,0,0,,What a place to find Illdoren!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.78,0:01:21.43,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Wha... What...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.81,0:01:24.86,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,What are these little things?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.86,0:01:27.44,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I can see why you'd be surprised, Sera.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.94,0:01:32.80,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Veor! Where have you been since supper?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.80,0:01:35.39,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Actually, what are these little things?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.39,0:01:37.01,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Now, now, there'll be time for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.01,0:01:39.95,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,You're going to see something even \Nmore surprising, soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.66,0:01:45.14,Main,Balhath,0,0,0,,So, this is the girl, Thundering Voice?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.41,0:01:51.16,Main,Karka,0,0,0,,The one who defended people \Nfrom the Tsukebikeshi?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.16,0:01:54.79,Main,Guas,0,0,0,,It takes real grit to \Nface a dragon head on.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.79,0:01:57.34,Main,Guas,0,0,0,,I can see why she's \NThundering Voice's bride.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.34,0:01:59.96,Main,Yufa,0,0,0,,Being thankful for that's part \Nof why we're having this party.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.96,0:02:01.60,Main,Vyufmec,0,0,0,,It's a party! A party!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.88,0:02:05.55,Main,Nimhala,0,0,0,,We've brought some of the \NSacred Tree's special liquor!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.55,0:02:07.48,Main,Fairies,0,0,0,,Yay!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.11,0:02:18.61,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,Tiny people with wings, animated plants,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.95,0:02:21.37,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,it's all so out of this world...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.94,0:02:24.60,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,How bad are my hallucinations \Ngoing to get?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.63,0:02:30.37,Main,Vas,0,0,0,,Findin' a wife so soon is a \Nreal cause for celebration!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.37,0:02:32.35,Main,Vas,0,0,0,,It's the guidance of the Great Spirits!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.95,0:02:37.13,Main,Vas,0,0,0,,Got somethin' for ya. \NMy way of sayin' congratulations.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.44,0:02:40.89,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Wh-Why would you give me something \Nas expensive as a sword?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.25,0:02:43.10,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Just be gracious and take it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.10,0:02:45.39,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The swords from his forge \Nare all masterpieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.61,0:02:47.57,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,That's not the issue!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.21,0:02:52.73,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,If you're not convinced, take a look at \Nthe blade. You'll want to keep it then.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.98,0:02:56.84,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,The blade? I mean, I can discern \Na sword's quality well enough...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.18,0:03:01.50,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Incredible.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.50,0:03:03.01,Main,Vas,0,0,0,,She's a beaut, ain't she?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.90,0:03:06.76,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,The blade itself is so consistent, \Nwithout a single distortion,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.09,0:03:10.67,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,while being just thick enough, \Nwith tasteful decorative fluting...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.82,0:03:16.94,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Is it enchanted? Balanced expertly \Naround the hilt, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.94,0:03:19.00,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Not a single flaw... the wrapping
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.46,0:03:22.34,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,on the grip is so smooth and almost \Nseems to cling to the hand...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.34,0:03:25.76,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,But more than anything, it gives \Noff this faint glow, like a pearl.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.47,0:03:27.75,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,It's beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.27,0:03:32.83,Main,Got,0,0,0,,S'made from metal that only \Nwe work: true silver alloy.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.83,0:03:35.90,Main,Got,0,0,0,,I hear the folks out \Nwest call it "mythril."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.90,0:03:37.75,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Mythril...?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.93,0:03:43.28,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,As in the same metal told of in the \NLord of the Armlets and Terminal Saga?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.28,0:03:49.66,Main,Vas,0,0,0,,The same. In them western tall tales, \Nthey apparently call us dwarves.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.09,0:03:54.80,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,If I may, I'd like to make \Nthe introductions here
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.80,0:03:58.17,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,that I called you all in for, \Nas the future great chief.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:59.00,0:04:00.88,Main - Top,Veor,0,0,0,,These are the three wise \Nelders of the Quefto clan:
Dialogue: 1,0:04:00.88,0:04:04.30,Main - Top,Veor,0,0,0,,Elder Vas, Elder Guas, and Elder Balhath.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.17,0:04:04.30,Time/Setting,Sign,0,0,0,,{\3c&HDCF4F7&\move(140,80,-10,80)\an2\fs16\fscx80}Three Wise Elders of the Quefto
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.17,0:04:04.30,Time/Setting,Sign,0,0,0,,{\3c&HDCF4F7&\an2\fs16\move(232.667,342.667,82.667,342.667)}Elder Vas
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.17,0:04:04.30,Time/Setting,Sign,0,0,0,,{\3c&HDCF4F7&\an2\fs16\move(475,342.667,325,342.667)}Elder Guas
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.17,0:04:04.30,Time/Setting,Sign,0,0,0,,{\3c&HDCF4F7&\an2\fs16\move(686.667,332.667,536.667,332.667)}Elder Balhath
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.36,0:04:09.93,Time/Setting,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,0)\an8\move(308,78,530,78)\fs18\3c&HDEF7F7&}Ixt Rijutsushi\NKarka Roth
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.30,0:04:07.49,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,An Ixt Rijutsushi, Lord Karka Roth.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.64,0:04:09.93,Time/Setting,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,0)\an8\move(-85,76,130,76)\fs18\3c&HDEF7F7&}Bud of the Sacred Tree\NNimhala
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.49,0:04:09.93,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The Bud of the Sacred Tree, Lady Nimhala.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.93,0:04:17.31,Time/Setting,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(508.667,110)\an8\fs18\3c&HD9F5F3&}Great Chief of the Fairies\NVyufumec the Tornado\Nand her retinue
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.50,0:04:14.43,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The Great Chief of the Fairies, \NLady Vyufumec and her servants.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.26,0:04:21.25,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Elves, spirits, and even fairies...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.25,0:04:23.24,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Are you all right, Sera?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.75,0:04:30.45,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Well, it's just... I didn't expect \Nanything more fantastical than a dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.84,0:04:35.07,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Be that as it may, they clearly exist. \NThat's simply how it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.48,0:04:37.93,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Besides, they're not characters \Nfrom some fantasy story.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.93,0:04:39.71,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,They're our dear neighbors.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.94,0:04:48.74,Main,Karka,0,0,0,,You needn't feel so self-conscious.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.74,0:04:52.33,Main,Karka,0,0,0,,Those from the west always react the \Nsame way, so we're accustomed to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.05,0:04:58.06,Main,Vyufumec,0,0,0,,If anything, it's funny, so keep being \Nshocked! It goes well with the liquor.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.39,0:04:59.73,Main,Nimhala,0,0,0,,Illdoren.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.73,0:05:04.61,Main,Nimhala,0,0,0,,This leaf is good for overstimulation. \NHas a sedative effect.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.61,0:05:07.38,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Th-Thank you?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.38,0:05:10.01,Main,Nimhala,0,0,0,,Some people foam at the mouth \Nafter taking it, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.86,0:05:14.87,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,I can't deny their existence since \Nthey're right in front of me,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.87,0:05:18.88,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,but unlike dragons, being able to \Nconverse with them is... a lot to take in!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.65,0:05:22.35,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,This is a lot of new information, \Nconsidering I'd been fighting with
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.35,0:05:25.14,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,the eastern expedition for seven years.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.14,0:05:28.51,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Well, they make a point to avoid the west.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.01,0:05:31.89,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Why appear before me, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.89,0:05:33.94,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Didn't I tell you, earlier?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.94,0:05:35.81,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I arranged this meeting between
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.81,0:05:38.77,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,the elders of the various clans \Nso I could introduce you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.05,0:05:40.77,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Now that you mention it...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.34,0:05:45.15,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I can see how you might have forgotten, \Nafter the Tsukebikeshi attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.47,0:05:50.28,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The tribes they represent, along with us, \Nthe oldest tribe of Cornem,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.28,0:05:53.49,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,collectively form the Five Great Tribes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.81,0:05:56.53,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The great chief, who moderates \Nconflicts between the five,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.53,0:06:00.57,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,is chosen in a ritual \Nby the great spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.41,0:06:04.36,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,All manner of peoples, big and small, \Nare born in this land,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.36,0:06:07.95,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,raised here, and live here, \Nbefore returning to the soil.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.31,0:06:10.46,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,We have joined hands with each other
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.46,0:06:13.68,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,because we all understand \Nthis course of nature.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.68,0:06:15.66,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The Tribal Alliance.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.66,0:06:18.11,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,That's what those of us who \Nshare a united culture,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.11,0:06:19.47,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,under the Great Spirits, are called.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.01,0:06:23.07,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,The Tribal Alliance...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.56,0:06:25.45,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,Then the barbarians... no,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.45,0:06:28.07,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,all these different races share \Nan equal cultural sphere?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.07,0:06:31.65,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Granted, unless there's \Nsome kind of crisis...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.57,0:06:35.43,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,we're mostly just drinking \Nbuddies, as you can see!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.83,0:06:40.04,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,This sounds more like a \Nparty than an alliance.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.33,0:06:45.71,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Wait, you spoke of crisis. \NWhat about Illodren's Eastern Expedition?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.83,0:06:50.34,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Why are you laughing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.48,0:06:55.71,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,You'll have to forgive us, we don't \Nmean to make light of your question.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.18,0:06:58.27,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,But the Tribal Alliance
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.27,0:07:02.51,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,doesn't get involved in territorial \Ndisputes in the first place.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.51,0:07:06.99,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Uh... do you mean to tell me \Nthat our war is being treated
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.99,0:07:09.87,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,with the same gravity as animals \Nfighting over territory?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.87,0:07:13.11,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,We're not all that different from \Nanimals, in the first place.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.11,0:07:14.42,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Besides, this alliance
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.42,0:07:18.00,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,wasn't created with the purpose of \Nsuppressing other peoples in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.27,0:07:20.09,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,What is it for, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.63,0:07:22.88,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,To respond to the threat of dragons?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.88,0:07:25.14,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Not that, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.14,0:07:29.51,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Our individual tribes can handle \Nmost beasts and dragons.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.86,0:07:32.33,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Then there's some greater threat
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.33,0:07:34.01,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,that requires you to \Nseek each other's aid?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.57,0:07:36.89,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I don't want you to misunderstand.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.89,0:07:40.43,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Dragons are, without a question, \Nboth clever and fierce.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.43,0:07:42.90,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,However, they are not dreadful.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.90,0:07:44.40,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Dreadful...?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.40,0:07:48.54,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,There is a type of monster... \Nwe call them Fiends.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.54,0:07:50.68,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,As you live here, you'll \Nencounter them sooner or later.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.68,0:07:53.38,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,They're a bit like a living disaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.38,0:07:54.42,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Fiends...?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.42,0:07:55.92,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Compared to fighting those things,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.92,0:07:57.88,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I would die with a smile on \Nmy face fighting Illdoren.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.88,0:07:59.66,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,What?! That is genuinely scary!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.66,0:08:02.93,Main,Vyufumec,0,0,0,,Okay, enough! No more!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.93,0:08:06.43,Main,Vyufumec,0,0,0,,If we keep talking about those \Nblights, I'm gonna feel sick!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.43,0:08:08.67,Main,Vyufumec,0,0,0,,I thought this was a celebration!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.27,0:08:11.55,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,She's right! Let's drink \Nand forget all about them!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.55,0:08:12.53,Main,Karka,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.94,0:08:14.80,Main,Vas,0,0,0,,A toast, to the new bride!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.29,0:08:18.87,Main,Nimhala,0,0,0,,Here you go! I hope you enjoy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.11,0:08:24.21,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The Kufuwek have the most vitality \Nout of all people of these lands.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.21,0:08:25.56,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Consider yourself lucky.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.56,0:08:27.39,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,O-Okay...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.39,0:08:30.63,Main,Guas,0,0,0,,We may be seeing Thundering Voice's \Nchild sooner than expected!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.07,0:08:33.48,Main,Balhath,0,0,0,,You give it your all, now!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.48,0:08:36.23,Main,Vas,0,0,0,,Her backside looks like she'll \Ngive him sturdy stock!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.23,0:08:37.45,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,B-Backside...?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.73,0:08:39.13,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Oh my!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.13,0:08:41.10,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Don't buy into their nonsense!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.87,0:08:46.44,Main,Karka,0,0,0,,You're already acting like a married \Ncouple of years! It's heartwarming.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.44,0:08:47.78,Main,Vyufumec,0,0,0,,I demand a smooch!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.78,0:08:51.05,Main - Top,Fairies,0,0,0,,Smooch him! Smooch him! Smooch him!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.05,0:08:54.22,Main - Top,Fairies,0,0,0,,Smooch him! Smooch him! Smooch him!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.38,0:08:52.39,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,There will be no smooches!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.39,0:08:54.22,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I'm surrounded by drunkards...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.14,0:08:57.19,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,It's their way of giving \Nus their blessings.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.19,0:08:59.97,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,They're as happy as they would \Nbe if it was their own joy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.92,0:09:04.49,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,It's not just the liquor, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.49,0:09:07.33,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The clothes and necklace \Nyou have are all gifts.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.67,0:09:12.28,Main,Vyufumec,0,0,0,,We spun your dress in our village.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.24,0:09:17.74,Main,Balhath,0,0,0,,The necklace is from us. \NA mix of gold and mythril!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.86,0:09:21.74,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,This, too? In addition to the sword?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.71,0:09:24.79,Main,Balhath,0,0,0,,This feller enchanted the sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.96,0:09:28.75,Main,Karka,0,0,0,,It repairs itself, so you'll never \Nneed to worry about maintenance.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.75,0:09:31.01,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,That sort of thing is possible?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.01,0:09:32.88,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,With Ixt sorcery, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.40,0:09:35.61,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,We all compensate for \Nthe things the others lack.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.61,0:09:38.54,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The Cornem, for example, \Noffer our combat strength
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.54,0:09:41.26,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,in exchange for the goods \Nand technology that we lack.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.26,0:09:42.87,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.35,0:09:48.19,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,This place truly is blessed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.15,0:10:01.83,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,My head hurts...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.50,0:10:04.12,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Are you awake?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.83,0:10:08.25,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Why would you bolt upright like that...?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.25,0:10:11.22,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I just... well... sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.22,0:10:15.00,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I came to wake you because the \Nelders had all returned home.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.00,0:10:16.84,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,It's already afternoon?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.10,0:10:21.95,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,Looking back on it now,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.95,0:10:27.07,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,it really was like I spent the night \Nin some sort of fairy tale...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.11,0:10:37.03,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,But it wasn't a fairy tale. It was real.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.42,0:10:40.91,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,It seems there's a great \Ndeal I've yet to learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.46,0:10:43.28,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Did you sleep well, Sera?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.70,0:10:48.29,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,Veor's beard?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.29,0:10:52.08,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,It grows back so quickly, I don't \Nusually bother with shaving, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.08,0:10:54.29,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,You're reacting the same way.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.29,0:10:56.53,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I-I have no idea what you mean!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.53,0:10:58.30,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Now, let's have lunch.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.21,0:11:02.05,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Wh-What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.33,0:11:05.31,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Eat now, flirt later.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.81,0:11:12.69,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,What is this? It's thick, and hot, \Nand kind of gamy... and juicy?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.42,0:11:15.94,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Dragon meat and herb sandwich, \Non potato loaf.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.37,0:11:18.74,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,It's from the Tsukebikeshi you killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.44,0:11:21.97,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Everyone else was eating it yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.37,0:11:23.57,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,The bird?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.57,0:11:24.70,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,It was a dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.37,0:11:29.37,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,It takes a moment to get used to, \Nbut it is quite good, that bird.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.37,0:11:30.57,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.57,0:11:32.27,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I'll take another.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.79,0:11:34.21,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,That's quite an appetite...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.21,0:11:37.21,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,We've got a bit of walking to do. \NAre you ready, Sera?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.96,0:11:43.27,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,There's someone who heard about you \Nthis morning and wants to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.27,0:11:45.22,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,An acquaintance of yours, apparently.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.28,0:11:55.02,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,I can't imagine who I \Nmight know around here...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.02,0:11:57.73,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,Someone I crossed blades with before?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.13,0:12:02.74,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,You could've waited in the house!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.44,0:12:08.74,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I was too excited to sit still.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.01,0:12:15.86,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,It has truly been a long \Ntime, Lady Serafina.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.21,0:12:19.38,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I heard you defended a family \Nthat was attacked by a dragon,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.69,0:12:21.18,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,and finding out
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.18,0:12:25.14,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,that you're as proud and courageous \Nas ever has me feeling nostalgic.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.11,0:12:28.23,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Sorry, who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.42,0:12:33.68,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Well, I have changed a fair bit...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.68,0:12:34.77,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I'm Nyleia.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.12,0:12:39.81,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I served as a knight in the Eastern \NExpedition under your command,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.81,0:12:40.98,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,four years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.98,0:12:42.56,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Do you remember me?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.56,0:12:44.65,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Nyleia from the Eastern Expedition...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.40,0:12:48.53,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Commander Lavillant.\NIt's a pleasure to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.35,0:12:50.83,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I am Nyleia de Philomar,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.24,0:12:55.29,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,at your service as a part of the Eastern \NExpeditionary Force's First Division.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.72,0:12:56.79,Flashback,Serafina,0,0,0,,Well met.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.53,0:13:01.69,Flashback,Serafina,0,0,0,,I've been told one of the frontier \Nvillages has come under attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.69,0:13:03.17,Flashback,Serafina,0,0,0,,Let's go, Nyleia!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.42,0:13:04.18,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.75,0:13:07.68,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Wretched barbarians. \NTheir struggle will be meaningless!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.17,0:13:13.40,Flashback,Serafina,0,0,0,,Are you all right, Nyleia?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.40,0:13:16.94,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I'm fine. But we need to \Npress them, quickly...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.85,0:13:24.39,Flashback,Serafina,0,0,0,,Nyleia!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.59,0:13:35.96,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Nyleia?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.96,0:13:39.06,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,My old subordinate, \N Viscount Philomar's daughter?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.06,0:13:40.71,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I thought you were dead!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.21,0:13:43.46,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I can see why you'd be surprised.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.46,0:13:47.47,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,And that belly... are you... with child?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.74,0:13:48.98,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,This will be my second.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.98,0:13:49.97,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,A second?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.97,0:13:53.08,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I mean, surely things can change \Na lot in four years, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.08,0:13:55.43,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,This is a bit too much \Nfor me to comprehend!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.70,0:14:01.59,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,It is a something of a long \Nstory... Let's talk inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.47,0:14:07.67,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,When my husband told me about \Nthe Crystal Helmet last night,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.67,0:14:08.99,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I thought it had to be you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.24,0:14:12.54,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,That helmet did tend to draw attention,\Nfor better or worse...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.54,0:14:14.37,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,And you have a husband, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.71,0:14:17.23,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I certainly do.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.23,0:14:20.36,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I was proposed to by the \Nman who defeated me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.36,0:14:22.63,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,And in spite of it all, \NI've made a life here...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.91,0:14:26.13,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I honestly have trouble \Nbelieving it at times.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.73,0:14:32.51,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,My time in the expeditionary force \Nfeels like another person's life.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.01,0:14:34.26,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.69,0:14:38.22,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I have to ask, why did \Nyou call out to Veor?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.22,0:14:41.07,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,He seems to be the son of \Nsomeone in authority...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.07,0:14:43.33,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Is it wise to have him \Nrunning errands for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.33,0:14:47.62,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,You'll find it's not quite the same \Nas in the west, in that sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.03,0:14:52.66,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,And young Veor stands out so much... \NI find myself turning to him for help.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.03,0:14:55.09,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,He does stand out, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.71,0:14:57.10,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,"Young" Veor?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.10,0:14:58.36,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,What is it, Sera?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.36,0:15:00.53,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,You're not that young.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.53,0:15:05.05,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Lady Serafina, Veor's only 18 years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.74,0:15:08.49,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,But have you seen his beard?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.49,0:15:11.42,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I can't help what my body does...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.65,0:15:15.71,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Lady Nyleia is my cousin's wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.71,0:15:17.68,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,So she's a distant relative.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.68,0:15:21.10,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,That's true. Being family is part of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.10,0:15:24.66,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Hang on, you're 18?! You?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.66,0:15:26.80,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Yes. Did I not mention that?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.80,0:15:27.95,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,You did not!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.95,0:15:30.20,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,And Lady Serafina turns 26 this—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.20,0:15:31.32,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Do not!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.22,0:15:37.45,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The prime of womanhood! \NThat suits me just fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.72,0:15:41.86,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I-I don't appreciate that statement \Nfrom someone younger than me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.25,0:15:45.96,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Or is that your way of \Nbragging about your youth?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.32,0:15:51.59,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,No. If anything, I wish \NI was born a bit earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.12,0:15:53.22,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.82,0:16:00.07,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I could've met you sooner, and you \Nwouldn't fret about the age difference.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.07,0:16:02.23,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Of all the ridiculous things to say...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.27,0:16:05.86,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Listen to me closely, Veor.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.51,0:16:10.52,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Don't assume our hypothetical alternate\Nencounter would end in your favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.52,0:16:14.36,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,No matter when, \NI will never be your bride!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.45,0:16:35.17,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,My lady, Serafina de Lavillant, \NI offer a heartfelt apology.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.59,0:16:37.39,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,The arrogance of my youth...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.66,0:16:40.77,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,was clearly an unintended insult \Nto you, a fellow warrior.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.74,0:16:43.64,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,As long as you understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.35,0:16:47.49,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Why did Master Veor randomly apologize?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.49,0:16:48.65,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.30,0:16:53.70,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,When Lady Serafina was captured, \Nwhat kind of injury did she have?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.70,0:16:56.20,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Nothing in particular.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.20,0:16:58.86,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,She managed to fight until \Nher sword shattered.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.17,0:17:01.41,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Then it wasn't shattered, but lasted \Nto the point of giving out...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.03,0:17:04.91,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Veor's in the wrong, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.04,0:17:07.30,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Listen well.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.30,0:17:10.50,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Knights make it a point of courtesy, \Nand warriors make it a point of pride,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.50,0:17:14.74,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,to fight to the death, with no mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.16,0:17:18.76,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,And when two foes are evenly matched,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.76,0:17:20.84,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,they fight until one is \Nno longer able to go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.43,0:17:27.81,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,But Veor, whose blows can \Nshatter stone and slay dragons,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.81,0:17:30.98,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,fought until her weapon, \Nwhich was ordinary steel, expired,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.98,0:17:33.07,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,yet was unable to land a single blow...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.07,0:17:36.35,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,In other words, it took an advantage in \Nequipment to let him fight her evenly,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.35,0:17:41.45,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,and beyond that, he had to rely on \Nhis stamina to draw out a victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.70,0:17:45.58,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,If he had left himself \Nopen for even a moment...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.51,0:17:55.31,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,All that said, war is about making do \Nwith the best weapons available to you,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.31,0:17:58.59,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,and he apparently didn't use \Nhis Thundering Voice, either...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.82,0:18:01.34,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Still, it's presumptuous to assume\N he'd win a second battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.34,0:18:04.13,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,considering it wasn't definitive \Nthe first time around.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.09,0:18:09.86,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I'm embarrassed enough. \NCould you show some mercy?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.86,0:18:11.54,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,He's never made that face before...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.54,0:18:14.11,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I can't believe I'm paying \Nsuch close attention to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.14,0:18:19.99,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I'd like to apologize again, Sera,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.28,0:18:23.87,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,as well as giving my thanks to \Nfortune for granting me my victory!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.34,0:18:26.37,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,F-Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.59,0:18:31.88,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,What was that?! She obviously likes him!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.88,0:18:33.90,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,I just wish they'd get on with it already.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.90,0:18:36.37,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,You two aren't mincing \Nwords anymore, are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.19,0:18:38.66,Main,Vidal/Erik,0,0,0,,We're back!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.21,0:18:41.39,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Oh, Vidal, welcome home.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.68,0:18:42.67,Main,Vidal,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.79,0:18:45.39,Main,Vidal,0,0,0,,Hey, it's Veo!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.85,0:18:48.89,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I'm too old to get called that, Vido.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.89,0:18:53.18,Main,Vidal,0,0,0,,Look at you, visiting with the \NCrystal Helmet and Cersei.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.18,0:18:54.58,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,Thanks for having us.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.58,0:18:56.15,Main,Vidal,0,0,0,,Make yourselves at home.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.94,0:19:01.14,Main,Erik,0,0,0,,Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.14,0:19:02.50,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Welcome home!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.50,0:19:05.64,Main,Vidal,0,0,0,,You should've seen him \Nout there running today.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.64,0:19:09.90,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Really? It won't be long before we'll \Nneed to get him a wooden sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.90,0:19:12.80,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Nyleia's husband and son...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.80,0:19:14.41,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,Lady Serafina.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.41,0:19:18.57,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I've accepted no shortage of scorn \Nfor becoming a knight as a woman...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.57,0:19:23.01,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,But serving and fighting under \Nyou has made something clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.18,0:19:27.10,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I was given a duty by God \Nto fight for my homeland.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.10,0:19:29.40,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,I will dedicate myself \Nto bettering the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.40,0:19:32.20,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,To claiming barbarian territory \Nand watering it with their savage blood,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.20,0:19:34.40,Flashback,Nyleia,0,0,0,,so that our crops may grow.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.39,0:19:38.60,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,You really have changed, Nyleia.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.41,0:19:45.03,Italics,Serafina,0,0,0,,But you look so much happier than \NI can ever remember you being...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.11,0:19:47.06,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,It's nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.73,0:19:51.41,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Oh, no! That was... I didn't mean to.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.41,0:19:53.04,Main,Cersei,0,0,0,,You didn't mean to...?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.04,0:19:55.23,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I didn't mean what I said, is all.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.23,0:19:56.04,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Sera?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.33,0:20:00.13,Main,Nyleia,0,0,0,,The Frozen Lavillant looks \Nhot under the collar...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.13,0:20:02.36,Main,Vidal,0,0,0,,Reminds me of when we were newlyweds!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.36,0:20:06.69,Main,Vidal,0,0,0,,This calls for celebratory drinks. \NI hope you're ready, Veo!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.06,0:20:09.42,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Newlyweds?! I'm not...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.29,0:20:19.07,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,I didn't expect to be \Ncelebrating two days in a row.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.05,0:20:24.48,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,These two days have made \Nsomething abundantly clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.48,0:20:28.45,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I knew nothing about this place.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.79,0:20:32.46,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Who lives here, what kind \Nof culture they have...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.75,0:20:37.21,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I marched, and fought against them, \Nwithout knowing any of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.21,0:20:42.95,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Your warriors have families, \Njust like the knights of Illdoren...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.51,0:20:48.30,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,But I didn't think of it, \Nand tried to ignore the obvious fact.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.77,0:20:50.97,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I called you barbarians and savages.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.69,0:20:54.20,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Using that as justification \Nfor an invasion,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.20,0:20:56.52,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,acting as if it was morally righteous...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.52,0:20:59.08,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Believing it was what \Nwas best for my people.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.86,0:21:03.93,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Sera...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.93,0:21:07.24,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I thought you were an \Nenemy, worthy of hate.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.64,0:21:11.49,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,But knowing you as a person, \Nit's clear that's wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.73,0:21:18.00,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,But even then... I am a knight, \Nand a noble of Illdoren.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.50,0:21:23.30,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,My yearning to save my barren homeland\Nand its suffering people remains.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.82,0:21:28.76,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,If I take home what I've learned here, \NI may be able to make that happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.77,0:21:33.52,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Which is why I have no intention \Nof becoming your wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.47,0:21:36.02,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,That stands to reason...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.82,0:21:40.27,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Still, that is only how I \Nfeel in light of my duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.54,0:21:45.47,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Which is to say, uh... well...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.91,0:21:51.03,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,Speaking as an individual, \NI don't think it sounds bad... Veor.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.83,0:21:54.04,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Sera!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.85,0:21:56.76,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,This is too much!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.76,0:22:02.02,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,You know, I'm certain now. For all \Nyour sincerity, you don't play fair.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.02,0:22:04.20,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,How was that not fair?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.70,0:22:07.56,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,You're not even aware of it... \NWhat a state of affairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.56,0:22:09.41,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,What are you on about?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.97,0:22:12.94,Sign_Basic,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an9\fad(750,0)\shad0\fs11\bord1\c&HBACBD0&\3c&H506972&\b1\blur1\pos(616,10)}Translation: Lee Francis\N\NTiming: Andy Ellis\N\NEditing: Zachary Carlysle\N\NQuality Control: Salem Alabanza\N\NTranslation Check: Sho Stifler
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.93,0:22:15.08,Main,Veor,0,0,0,,Another fine meal!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.08,0:22:16.93,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,You're in a good mood.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.93,0:22:20.94,Main - Top,Veor,0,0,0,,Well, can you blame me, after how \Ncharming you were last night?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.94,0:22:23.78,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,I-I wasn't trying to...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.78,0:22:26.06,Main - Top,Serafina,0,0,0,,It was the liquor talking!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.45,0:22:31.20,Main - Top,Veor,0,0,0,,Oh, I see. Then it's not \Nhow you truly feel...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.50,0:22:33.48,Main,Serafina,0,0,0,,You...!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.48,0:22:36.95,Main - Top,Serafina,0,0,0,,Do you think I'm shameless enough to say \Nsomething so brazen and not mean it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.31,0:22:40.63,Main - Top,Serafina,0,0,0,,What I said last night were \Nmy true and honest feelings!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.63,0:22:41.46,Main - Top,Serafina,0,0,0,,Do not insult me!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.71,0:22:44.46,Main - Top,Cersei,0,0,0,,And now she's saying it without any booze.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.31,0:22:49.72,Main - Top,Veor,0,0,0,,To be so honest while sober... \Nit's really unfair how lovely you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.87,0:22:53.97,Main - Top,Serafina,0,0,0,,You said the same thing yesterday!
